since first appearing on screen in  2018's black panther the african nation  of wakanda has become one of the most  iconic settings in the mcu  but what's the real story behind  t'challa's homeland this is the history  of wakanda  explained everyone knows wakanda as the  civilization that discovered vibrania  the true origins of the country however  are far more complicated than that  and are rooted in a deep and mysterious  mysticism  wakanda was originally home to a  collection of beasts known as the  originators  among these ancient creatures were  beings such as the serpentine symbi  the ape-like vanion the arachnoid anansi  and the insectoid swarm  known as the creeping doom eventually  ancient human beings were drawn to the  area where they soon encountered these  strange beasts  they all lived in harmony for a while  but the originators balked when humans  started to abuse the land's natural  resources  a deadly conflict ensued and among the  human combatants arose heroes that  ascended to become the gods of wakanda  otherwise known as the urisha with the  help of the urisha  the originators were defeated and  banished to the nether realms forever  losing the land they had called home  wakanda was founded shortly after for  years the country developed pretty much  just like any other ancient civilization  but soon enough thanks to a little  cosmic mischief a rock from outer space  would land in wakanda  one that would forever change the marvel  universe  in the early days of wakanda the  country's ancient denizens learned to  manipulate storm clouds  in order to funnel cosmic energy for  their own ends  but this practice had an unintended side  effect it caused the wakandans to pull  down a meteor from space  this meteor contained a metal that  absorbed both sound and energy  which the world would later come to call  vibranium  the first tribe to be brave enough to  investigate the meteor crash site was  led by bashanga  wakanda's biggest and baddest warrior  bushenga immediately saw the value of  this new substance and decided to put it  to use in his tribe's weapons giving  them an edge over their foes  nowadays vibranium is one of the most  important aspects of the marvel universe  for one thing it's what captain  america's shield is constructed from the  most versatile substance on the planet  and they used it to make a frisbee but  the use of this metal helped modern  wakanda become the beacon of  technological advancement that it is  today  not to mention the most well-defended  country on the planet  while the benefits of vibranium are  clear its discovery set off a chain of  events that would forever change the  landscape of the world  it also ushered in a series of  unintended and deadly consequences  although bashanga's brutal methods may  have seemed suited towards a simpler  more primitive time he ended up being  one of the most important figures in  wakandan history  bushenga first believed the vibranium  meteor to be a gift from the gods  unfortunately his tribe quickly found  that exposure to untreated vibranium can  mutate living things on earth  into grotesque monsters which they named  demon spirits  in order to combat these new foes  bashanga prayed to the panther god to  give him the strength to defeat them  thus making him the first of the proper  black panthers  basically if you were born in ancient  wakanda and ended up being exposed to a  little too much vibranium there was a  good chance you'd turn into a monster  and a super powered panther would show  up and beat the living hell out of you  now it was later revealed that there had  actually been a prehistoric black  panther  but the lineage that ends with king  t'challa got its start with bashanga's  battles against the demon spirits  eventually bashanga united the region's  various tribes  and formed the singular nation of  wakanda  the radiation from the vibranium meteor  didn't just affect people though  it also had an impact on the flora and  fauna of the surrounding area  hence the special herbs that black  panthers consumed to give them their  powers  after becoming the first black panther  bashango recognized the destructive  power of the vibranium meteor  and closed it off to the rest of the  kingdom in the process  he also established the black panther  cult who swore to use the powers of the  meteor to protect the people of wakanda  and stop the demon spirits from  spreading but while wakanda's black  panther cult is obviously the most  prominent  it's not the only one and the wakandans  worship a number of other animal gods  these groups include the lion cult the  crocodile cult the hyena clan  and the most dangerous of all the white  gorilla cult  t'challa's rival imbaku who is otherwise  known as man abe  would lead the people of his village in  consuming the flesh of the mutated white  gorillas of the region  gaining their super strength for  themselves mbaku would eventually use  this power to overthrow the black  panther  and briefly take the throne of wakanda  for himself if the world found out what  we truly are what we possess  we could lose our way of life throughout  history  many have tried to invade wakanda and  many have failed too  all kinds of armies ranging from the  romans to the knights templar  to hordes of demons from hell have made  their way to the region  and were each thoroughly beaten back  however  in the 1800s the country faced its  greatest threat yet  led by the belgian colonel named claw a  group of white soldiers targeted the  area after an otherwise successful  conquest of south africa  luckily they were no match for the  wakandan technology which caused their  guns to misfire  colonel claw himself was killed during  the invasion but that wasn't the last  wakanda had seen of the claw family  unfortunately for the wakandans claw had  an equally deplorable sun  and when world war ii came around  colonel fritz claw couldn't join the  nazis fast enough  he made his way to wakanda in an attempt  to impress hitler  only to be welcomed by the then current  black panther king azuri  and shown the secrets of its vibranium  then when his real intentions became  clear  claude jr was beaten back to germany but  this event put wakanda firmly in the  crosshairs of both the axes and allies  that's when azuri and his son t'chaka  enlisted the help of captain america to  keep the nazis led by baron strucker and  the red skull from taking over the  country  the battle against the nazis was the  first modern invasion that wakanda had  fought  and against a technologically advanced  and highly knowledgeable enemy no less  it was this war that taught a young  t'chaka of the dangers of the outside  world  and how desperately they coveted  wakanda's secrets  many stories that involved the black  panther tend to pick up during the reign  of t'chaka  largely because he was perhaps the most  important ruler the country had seen up  to that point  certainly king t'chaka was a significant  influence on the country's decision to  keep itself cut off from the world  raised in the turbulent times of world  war ii t'chaka saw what happens when the  outside world discovers wakanda for what  it truly is and how it almost  always ends with the spilling of  wakandan blood his solution was to  conceal wakanda from the outside world  tricking everyone into thinking it had  no more to offer than any other african  country  t'chaka would sell a little vibranium  technology here and there  in order to keep the lights on while at  the same time secretly developing the  country's sharpest minds  to this end t'chaka developed a system  in which wakanda would send its best  and brightest to study abroad so that  they could bring their knowledge back to  wakanda  and help it thrive in secrecy  unfortunately things fell apart when  ulysses s  claw a descendant of the belgian colonel  led an assassination mission into  wakanda  during claws attack t'chaka was killed  protecting his young son t'challa  in return t'challa avenged his father by  shattering claw's right arm  in the comics when t'chaka died t'challa  was just 13 years old  far too young to take the throne as per  wakandan customs his uncle sian  performed the ritual  and became the next black panther acting  as king region in his nephew's stead  while sayon kept things in check  t'challa went to study in europe and the  united states  he would eventually gain a phd in  physics from oxford university  before finally coming of age and  returning to wakanda to take his  rightful place on the throne  t'challa's homecoming was briefly  waylaid by the organization known as aim  who captured him while he was looking  for the heart-shaped herb that would  give him the power of the black panther  luckily he managed to escape with the  help of a childhood friend and went on  to beat his uncle in the infamous  wakandan combat ritual  once all was said and done t'challa had  gained the superhuman powers of the  black panther  as well as the heavy responsibility of  ruling his secret kingdom  many of the early black panther stories  involved t'challa grappling with his  loyalty to his father's legacy as  wakanda grows and prospers  having developed new kinds of technology  and welcomed a number of new superheroes  the country eventually became  impossible to hide under king t'challa  wakanda finally revealed itself to the  world  we must find a way to look after one  another  as if we were one single  tribe one of the most infamous events in  marvel history is the secret invasion  which saw an alien race known as the  skrulls attempt to invade earth by  posing as the planet's key leaders and  heroes  inevitably the skrulls quickly  identified wakanda's importance  and wasted no time in infiltrating the  country fortunately black panther got  wise to their ruse and took steps to  ensure that he could pull a fast one on  the invaders  eventually things came to a head and the  scroll 